    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog centers on exploiting a favorable matchup against R. Johnson, whose high xERA makes our top-tier bats must-starts. **Bryce Harper** (77.13) sits atop our projected leaderboard, benefiting from a soft matchup and elite xwOBA metrics that anchor the heart of our lineup. **Lawrence Butler** (73.46) also provides elite upside; while he faces a tougher arm in Baz, his dynamic platoon advantage and current park factors make him a high-efficiency engine for run production. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.93) continues to offer consistent, high-floor output against a left-handed arm, proving that his pedigree remains immune to standard platoon-split concerns.\n\nOur peripheral speed assets remain critical to securing the scarcest category in this 5x5 format. **Justin Crawford** (64.16) is a vital start for stolen base potential despite a lower-order lineup assignment that suppresses his raw daily score. We are keeping a close watch on **Luis Arraez** (66.77) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.64), both of whom benefit significantly from the projected SP weakness and favorable wind conditions, respectively. The most difficult bench decision involved **Gleyber Torres** (55.51). He narrowly missed the cut because, despite a strong projection against a lefty, the matchup against Snell presents too much volatility compared to the steadier floors offered by **Braden Montgomery** and **Dylan Beavers**, whose underlying efficiency metrics currently outpace the aggregate value of the bench.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our \"Lineup Pending\" designations. We are operating on the assumption that **Bryce Harper**, **Luis Arraez**, and **Justin Crawford** will occupy their predicted spots; should any of these veterans hit the bench or slide down the order, their efficiency scores will shift immediately. Furthermore, while **Cal Raleigh** (58.96) remains a solid play, his dynamic platoon penalty against a right-hander keeps his ceiling modest. We are proceeding with the current configuration to maximize our SB floor while maintaining a comfortable buffer against the higher-tier arms on today\u2019s schedule.",
